{"title":"2005 iTest Problems/Problem 5","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/e/fdecf1a0969debea5ce83f98ee698d917d5756f0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 30^\\circ + \\sin 45^\\circ + \\sin 60^\\circ + \\sin 90^\\circ + \\cos 120^\\circ + \\cos 135^\\circ + \\cos 150^\\circ + \\cos 180^\\circ = ?$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"639\" height=\"16\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The trigonometric values above can be quickly found on the unit circle, and are values that you should memorize. We will find one as an example, and the rest can be found by the reader. The sine of 30 degrees is the <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/9/2/092e364e1d9d19ad5fffb0b46ef4cc7f2da02c1c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"11\" height=\"13\" />-coordinate of the point on the unit circle that makes an angle of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/1/9/919bf5d461970fc8d905d63704ef763c08594184.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30^\\circ$\" width=\"24\" height=\"13\" /> with the horizontal. Dropping the altitude from that point to the x-axis gives us a <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/c/47c78b85058ee5e17f88e2cde302e48aad826b35.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$30-60-90$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"101\" height=\"15\" /> right triangle. Since the hypotenuse is 1, the y-coordinate of the point is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />. Therefore, the sine of 30 degrees is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/9/2/192b4a258ee998961a99523fd0f0a029f9ea194a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5$\" width=\"22\" height=\"12\" />. Repeating this process for the other values, we finally plug in. Our answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/e/f/aef8b47fe572630e544fa43e1c455d5835982f31.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$0.5+\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}+\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}+1-0.5-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}-1=\\boxed{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"329\" height=\"43\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2005_iTest_Problems/Problem_5&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/4/1/f41470508df2ceb87f97c7e939589024bceb16e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{x}$\" width=\"35\" height=\"12\" /> is an odd function and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/5/7/5575daca0dbe5b13fe9ccccf4853c11c7be1f720.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\cos{x} = \\sin{90^{\\circ} - x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"148\" height=\"16\" />, we have:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/5/b45e6ce2e599cadf744143a75f203fca8edee6e9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin 30^\\circ + \\sin 45^\\circ + \\sin 60^\\circ + \\sin 90^\\circ + \\cos 120^\\circ + \\cos 135^\\circ + \\cos 150^\\circ + \\cos 180^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"611\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/a/9/3a955a066b05a19a6f2c5b554af6af16a0d60b39.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\sin 30^\\circ + \\sin 45^\\circ + \\sin 60^\\circ + \\sin 90^\\circ + \\sin -30^\\circ + \\sin -45^\\circ + \\sin -60^\\circ + \\sin -90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"642\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/c/68c73c1a7cfc4906269d1a2ea54c55782af6df3c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\sin 30^{\\circ} + \\sin 45^{\\circ} + \\sin 60^{\\circ} + \\sin 90^{\\circ} - \\sin 30^\\circ - \\sin 45^\\circ - \\sin 60^\\circ - \\sin 90^\\circ$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"586\" height=\"16\" />\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/b/d/abdb407f58a63c2e882b288f4783c4ad830e5af9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$=\\boxed{0}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -6px\" width=\"41\" height=\"25\" />\n</p><p>~anabel.disher\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</s